Hi all,
I'm using the below code to try and grab the terms that have the greatest sums of field "impression":

{
"size":0,
"query":{
"filtered":{
"query":{"match_all":{}},
"filter":{
"and":{
"filters":[{"range":{"date_time":{"from":"2013-12-12T00:00:00Z","to":"2013-12-12T23:59:59Z"}}}]
} 
}
}
},
"aggs":{
"XXXXXXXXX" : {
"terms" : { 
"field" : "XXXXXXXXX.untouched",
"size" : 10,
"order" : { "Impression_summation" : "desc" }
},
"aggs" : {
"Impression_summation" : { "sum" : { "field" : "impression" } }
}
}
}
}}
'

While this code _does_ order by the sums of that field, it is omitting many terms that would have even greater sums. It is only after I increase the size parameter to something pretty high (10 --> 1000 in this case), does it then 'catch' the terms with the largest summations of field "impression". Is there other code I should be using for this or is this a bug? Thanks!
